From 70444e41f354a006eb26f08ac292cdd54b690321 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:03:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(host-contracts): ACL v0.4.2 backport of the E1
 successor extension (lifecycle Level 2)

Same E1 code as main's ACL v0.9.0 (lifecycle/level2 50147ff): the
Succession record and the raise-only delay appended to the retirement
namespace, designate / mandatory accept / confirm after D = 7 days /
locked, retirement voids pending designations and emits the confirmed
successor, and the delegated view answers for (account, successor) after
retirement as an active, non-expiring wildcard delegation would. This line
has no isDelegatedForUserDecryption view. On this line the gateway verifies
the delegate's ECDSA signature, so a successor must be an ECDSA EOA.

Version 0.4.1 -> 0.4.2, reinitializer 6 -> 7, reinitializeV6(). Level 0
upgrade tests run against an ACL v0.4.1 fixture (make_fixtures.py, blob
57bc6f5c); new U8 tests cover v0.4.1 -> v0.4.2, v0.4.0 -> v0.4.2,
reinitializeV6 and a Core-only rollback (fail-closed, record kept).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
